that you're hearing out there.

01:11:46.680 --> 01:11:48.608
Thank you so much,
[? Kuko, ?] for all

01:11:48.608 --> 01:11:49.650
that you're doing for us.

01:11:54.050 --> 01:11:55.800
And you met him at the top.

01:11:55.800 --> 01:11:58.250
But I really have to think
John Harbison for all

01:11:58.250 --> 01:12:05.320
he's done for this
semester stepping

01:12:05.320 --> 01:12:10.150
in for Herb and really, for
decades of love and attention

01:12:10.150 --> 01:12:13.690
that he's given to the
MIT musical community.

01:12:13.690 --> 01:12:15.010
He's such a great asset.

01:12:15.010 --> 01:12:17.560
And if you find him,
show him your love.

01:12:17.560 --> 01:12:21.430
He's really such an
asset to all of us.

01:12:21.430 --> 01:12:23.188
And, Fred, thank you.

01:12:23.188 --> 01:12:23.980
Thank you for this.

01:12:23.980 --> 01:12:26.390
I know you're out
there somewhere.

01:12:26.390 --> 01:12:27.820
Oh, he's back there, OK.

01:12:31.650 --> 01:12:33.442
It's been a great pleasure.

01:12:33.442 --> 01:12:36.570
[INAUDIBLE]

01:12:36.570 --> 01:12:38.980
OK, this is "Un Poco Loco."

01:12:38.980 --> 01:12:39.480
Thanks.

01:12:56.446 --> 01:12:59.939
One, one, one, one.

01:12:59.939 --> 01:13:02.434
[MUSIC - "UN POCO LOCO"]

01:19:02.900 --> 01:19:04.896
[APPLAUSE]

01:19:34.190 --> 01:19:35.580
Thank you so much for coming.

01:19:35.580 --> 01:19:40.820
And we will be
playing again May 9,

01:19:40.820 --> 01:19:43.190
although with a different
team, I believe.

01:19:43.190 --> 01:19:48.222
Laura, Jay, will be I think,
running the show at that point.

01:19:48.222 --> 01:19:49.680
Thank you so much
again for coming,

01:19:49.680 --> 01:19:51.180
and we'll see you next time.

01:19:51.180 --> 01:19:51.780
Bye bye.

01:19:51.780 --> 01:19:54.530
[APPLAUSE]

